(BUF-48: after `Free`, all four resize spellings — `resize`,
 `reallocate`, `grow`, `shrink` — are also refused with the error flag.
 Not itself enumerated by the "Releasing a Buffer" prose (LANGUAGE.md
 3630-3634 names reads/writes generally, not the resize keywords by
 name); hand-verified to hold, consistent with the general
 read-or-write-refused contract.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox BUF-48.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   resize refused
   reallocate refused
   grow refused
   shrink refused
)
a buffer called buf1 is "one".
Free buf1.
resize buf1 to 16.
On error print "resize refused".

a buffer called buf2 is "two".
Free buf2.
reallocate buf2 to 16.
On error print "reallocate refused".

a buffer called buf3 is "three".
Free buf3.
grow buf3 to 16.
On error print "grow refused".

a buffer called buf4 is "four".
Free buf4.
shrink buf4 to 16.
On error print "shrink refused".
